okay let's get right into audience  questions for the week there are some  good ones first one hey David did you  see bob lazar on Joe Rogan are his  claims about UFOs credible do you  believe him I did see this and I watched  this with great interest so if you're  not familiar with this there's a guy  named Bob Lazar who was on Joe Rogan's  program a week or two ago and Bob Lazar  is now about 60 years old and he says  he's a physicist that he worked on  extraterrestrial technology including  flying saucers he were trying to reverse  engineer this supposedly alien  technology at a place near called s4  near the area 51 location in the United  States Southwest and not only was he on  Joe Rogan recently there's a Netflix  documentary about him now and I watched  the documentary and I watched the  interview on Joe Rogan and what's  stunning and interesting about this  particular guy compared to some other  UFO people making claims about UFOs and  extraterrestrial technology is that he  is so easily able to talk about what  seemed like such specific details that  would be really difficult to make up  like if he didn't really do this stuff  if he didn't really see this stuff it  would be hard for him to so articulately  and specifically and consistently talk  about this material he says very clearly  what he does remember and things that he  doesn't remember him sometimes people  say you know if he was just making it up  he would always have answers or it would  seem more difficult for him to recall  supposed details he was really specific  about where was he and wasn't he allowed  into when he was working at this  location he explains in great detail how  gravity fields and element 115 and all  sorts of things work and I admit it's  interesting and it's compelling to watch  him talk about it in the documentary and  with Joe Rogan but I got a ton of people  asking me do I believe the substance of  what he says because he seems so  convincing and if it's true then the  government has been carrying out this  massive cover-up operation about the  fact that we have alien spacecraft and  technologies that are not of this world  which would be a massive massive  revelation and a scandal and say  as a sort of defense of a lot of the  things that Bob Lazar talked about more  generally in terms of technology include  things that he talked about which have  since become realities or have been sort  of he's been vindicated hand scanners  elements of wave theory have been proven  true over the years and in the  documentary he also says that he was  raided by the FBI  while the documentary itself was in  production which would again suggest  that there is a government effort to  cover up his ability to tell the story  the truth about what he's been involved  in now it's important to recognize that  there's no actual evidence or paperwork  or video or anything that confirms law  enforcement was at his place or raided  him I mean nothing is presented and I  think that's an important starting point  for our conversation so in the end I  don't believe the specifics of what Bob  Lazar is saying and I want to be clear  I'm not saying that we are alone in the  universe I don't know that to be true  mathematically there's a very compelling  case for there being alien life  elsewhere in the universe that's not  what I'm saying what I'm saying is that  the Bob Lazar claims for me have very  quickly become sort of these  conspiracies conspiracy things where  absence of evidence is interpreted as  actual evidence so as an example there's  no evidence of the FBI raid that he  claims happened this is seen by those  who believe Bob Lazar that clearly the  raid happened and was covered up and all  evidence of it was removed Occam's razor  would suggest that he simply made it up  the simplest explanation for why there  was no evidence for that raid is that it  didn't happen along the same lines  there's no evidence that Bob Lazar went  to school at the places he claims he  went to school the documentary and the  Rogen interview suggests that he did get  these degrees from the places he claims  but in order to discredit him there's  been a campaign to erase all evidence of  him having attended those schools  transcripts and admissions records were  deleted people who attended the schools  at the time he claims to be there  been gotten to and that's why they're  saying they have no recollection of Bob  Lazar going there it's a cover-up to  hide the fact that he's really educated  in physics again Occam's razor suggests  that the simplest explanation is the  best one which is he simply made it up  there's no record of him having attended  those schools because he didn't when you  go further and you look into Bob  lazarre's claims about gravity and  whatever else there are plenty of actual  people we know to be physicists who  debunked the stuff that he says now I  can't possibly debunk every scientific  claim Bob Lazar makes nor would it be  relevant because people who believed it  would just come up with new explanations  as to why he's believable but as an  example Lazar claims that one of his  vindications is that science has now  determined gravity to be a wave which  he's been saying for a long time and a  lot of the stuff he says about the alien  propulsion systems depend on that actual  physicists just don't agree with that  premise they say there is one theory  about gravity general relativity which  says gravity is neither a particle nor a  wave there are things called  gravitational waves but actual  physicists widely say that even the way  that Bob Lazar was setting up the  conversation about gravity is wrong but  when you watch it it seems so compelling  and he seems so articulate about this  stuff that people do get pulled in so  long story short without diagnosing  anyone I've spoken to my dad about this  extensively who's a mental health  professional and generally about these  not about Bob Lazar specifically but  I've spoken to him generally about these  folks who sound so smart and they seem  so grounded and yet they talk about  these wild topics but seems so normal  without anything else unusual going on  with them you talk to them about sports  or politics or whatever and they just  seem with it why is it that they  wouldn't be believable about this one  area whether it's aliens or whatever  else there's a condition called para  Freni a-- okay that might apply to some  of these folks I'm not even pretending  to diagnose Bob Lazar I'm merely telling  you there is a condition that explained  this and para Frannie as a condition  which is characterized by a very  organized system of delusions that  sometimes include paranoia sometimes  there are hallucinations often auditory  and sometimes there are not so you don't  even need to believe or argue about  whether the person believes the things  they say themselves or they're just  making it up para Freni a-- notably  doesn't come with that deteriorating  intellect or the personality issues that  lots of schizophrenic people do  experience when schizophrenic people get  serious schizophrenia they often start  to behave in ways that generally don't  make sense you meet them you can't have  a conversation with them about sports or  politics or whatever their entire  intellect and personality become  compromised with para Freni a-- you will  much more commonly have people who don't  act strangely or hold bizarre out of  this world for lack of a better term  beliefs except for this one area and one  thing that is often a part of para Freni  ax is the belief of being persecuted  that paranoia also is is often common in  schizophrenia which is right there in  bob lazar story right he claims to have  been raided for the FBI there's no  evidence that that raid took place he  believes he's being surveilled he won't  talk about element 115 with an earshot  of phones that have the battery in them  because he believes that it's possible  that he is being surveilled there so to  be clear I'm not saying Bob Lazar is  para phrenic what I'm telling you is  that there are simpler explanations for  these things which sometimes should be  considered and I don't find Bob Lazar  story particularly compelling tell me  where I'm wrong one of today's sponsors  is impeach the card slap game you cannot  slap Donald Trump in real life but you  can slap him in this hilarious  fast-paced two-player card game and you  can get it for ten percent off when you  go to david pakman.com slash impeach and  use the coupon code pakman show at  checkout all one word awesome for  parties when you're having a few drinks  I've been playing it with some friends  of mine currently has a 5 out of 5 star  rating on  and it combines clever satire about the  Trump administration with really funny  high-quality cartoon artwork all in a  really lively card game that's easy to  learn but it stays interesting every  time you play it because of how well  designed it is and really how much  thought went into the humor and the  political commentary the game covers a  ton of themes global warming Russian  collusion tax cuts for the wealthy  impeach the cards slap game is perfect  if you're looking for something fun and  casual to do with your politically  minded friends or family members you  might even learn something new about the  Trump administration while you're  playing the game it's a perfect gift for  anyone who has a sense of humor about  Trump or get it for yourself and have a  really fun and witty game to play when  people come over you can even play it  tournament style get impeach the cards  slap game by going to david pakman.com  slash impeach and get 10% off when you  use the coupon code pakman show at  checkout all one word

